{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/561088-a-little-political-sidereal-guidance-in-the-campaign-i-am-in-please","id":561088,"title":"A little political Sidereal guidance in the campaign I am in please.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-06-19T13:30:39-07:00","id":561088,"title":"A little political Sidereal guidance in the campaign I am in please.","content":"I'm playing a Sidereal in a campaign and the character requested the help of an associate for a mission he was on. The price is sending a message to a localized neighborhood god (It's a gated community) in Paragon who has been acting up or causing some small troubles for the assocate (sidereal).<br /> <br /> I have a couple of ideas of what to do and I am unsure of how easy it would be to implement.<br /> <br /> My Sidereal is currently does not have a lot of social charms, my fault, and only has Icy Hand/Palm (the charm that makes bureaucrats do the right thing) and Fortuitous Fellowship.<br /> <br /> My first idea is to use Fortuitous Fellowship on the people living in that neighborhood/gated community to create a social policy against this local god, goading them to burn down his shrine. However, with the Paragonese oaths, how viable is this? Would the oaths prevent them burning down his shrine?<br /> <br /> 2. Find out everything that has gone wrong in that neighborhood, grab an unemployed city god in Yu-Shan and use Fortuitous Fellowship to build a cult for that god and set him up as a competing god. How much paperwork is there in offering that unemployed god such a cult or position, and what can the original god whose cult and domain are being cut into do about it?<br /> <br /> 3. This could maybe be factored into part of 2, but use Icy Hand to speed through any investigations of that particular god's actions and get him censured/rebuked.<br /> <br /> I am open to other ideas as well.<br /> <br /> Thank you,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3012-uknown-darklord","name":"Uknown DarkLord","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3012_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:03:16-07:00","id":561164,"title":"","content":"It would be pretty problematic to have them burn down his shrine, because then they would all suffer the effects of their oath and be in excruciating pain (or die) unless they presented to a magistrate. <br /> <br /> 2/3 are the better ideas, though you could use Fortuitous Fellowship to create a social policy to ostracize or not to pray to that god. That's less of a danger to the people than <i>inciting arson </i>which probably won't do much but piss the god off frankly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:03:20-07:00","id":561166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/561088-a-little-political-sidereal-guidance-in-the-campaign-i-am-in-please#post561088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm playing a Sidereal in a campaign and the character requested the help of an associate for a mission he was on. The price is sending a message to a localized neighborhood god (It's a gated community) in Paragon who has been acting up or causing some small troubles for the assocate (sidereal).</div> </div> </div> </div>Paragon or Chiaroscuro? Depending on the specific city your sidereal might be <b>very dead indeed</b> if he takes such agressive approaches to the matter...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I have a couple of ideas of what to do and I am unsure of how easy it would be to implement.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/561088-a-little-political-sidereal-guidance-in-the-campaign-i-am-in-please#post561088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Sidereal is currently does not have a lot of social charms, my fault, and only has Icy Hand/Palm (the charm that makes bureaucrats do the right thing) and Fortuitous Fellowship.<br /> <br /> My first idea is to use Fortuitous Fellowship on the people living in that neighborhood/gated community to create a social policy against this local god, goading them to burn down his shrine. However, with the Paragonese oaths, how viable is this? Would the oaths prevent them burning down his shrine?<br /> <br /> 2. Find out everything that has gone wrong in that neighborhood, grab an unemployed city god in Yu-Shan and use Fortuitous Fellowship to build a cult for that god and set him up as a competing god. How much paperwork is there in offering that unemployed god such a cult or position, and what can the original god whose cult and domain are being cut into do about it?<br /> <br /> 3. This could maybe be factored into part of 2, but use Icy Hand to speed through any investigations of that particular god's actions and get him censured/rebuked.<br /> <br /> I am open to other ideas as well.<br /> <br /> Thank you,</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, i know it is just a neighborhood god, but ain't your character being a little too eager to get itself in a serious conflict with a god it doesn't even know?<br /> The way you describe it, sounds more like &quot;break down its door, its legs, burn the house and salt the earth&quot; than &quot;sending a message&quot;.<br /> <br /> Wouldn't trying to find out who is this &quot;troublesome small god acting up&quot; first and why exactly did your associate not solve that itself instead of asking you to do so as payment?<br /> Maybe the god is a little bigger or influential than you're giving it credit for. Anyway, checking things first is always wise, imho.<br /> <br /> Good luck with this enterprise of yours!<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:05:42-07:00","id":561189,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Uknown DarkLord</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/561088-a-little-political-sidereal-guidance-in-the-campaign-i-am-in-please#post561088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My first idea is to use Fortuitous Fellowship on the people living in that neighborhood/gated community to create a social policy against this local god, goading them to burn down his shrine. However, with the Paragonese oaths, how viable is this? Would the oaths prevent them burning down his shrine?</div> </div> </div> </div>They absolutely will not prevent it, but they will punish anyone breaking the law in Paragon (by, say, committing arson) pretty harshly. If I were your GM I would require some fairly mammoth lifting to provoke a Paragonese population to riot; the Perfect has them very cowed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Find out everything that has gone wrong in that neighborhood, grab an unemployed city god in Yu-Shan and use Fortuitous Fellowship to build a cult for that god and set him up as a competing god. How much paperwork is there in offering that unemployed god such a cult or position, and what can the original god whose cult and domain are being cut into do about it? </div> </div> </div>I would advise against this. This isn't &quot;sending a message,&quot; this is &quot;starting a long-term, grueling turf war between rival deities.&quot; The deity in question might not even know why someone has started a turf war with him.<br /> <br /> Question; what exactly do you mean by &quot;sending a message&quot; here? That can mean anything from &quot;let this city god know he is on notice&quot; to &quot;murder the balls out of him.&quot; What are you expected to do here, exactly? Is it your responsibility to make the god stop acting up, or simply to threaten or cajole him and that fulfills your end of the deal?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I am open to other ideas as well. </div> </div> </div>Violence can work. This guy isn't even the City Father of Paragon, he's just some podunk neighborhood god, right? Slap on a Resplendency for disguise, walk into his sanctum, and comment on what a nice place it is, it would be a shame if anything were to happen to it. If he doesn't get the message, slap him around a little, make it clear if he doesn't play nice the next visit is going to involve broken kneecaps.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;SEX NOVA is the kind of person who, after being chosen as the divine champion of the god of heroes, decided to call himself SEX NOVA.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4742-murcushio","name":"Murcushio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4742_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1249"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:09:56-07:00","id":561198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Murcushio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/561088-a-little-political-sidereal-guidance-in-the-campaign-i-am-in-please?p=561189#post561189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Violence can work. This guy isn't even the City Father of Paragon, he's just some podunk neighborhood god, right? Slap on a Resplendency for disguise, walk into his sanctum, and comment on what a nice place it is, it would be a shame if anything were to happen to it. If he doesn't get the message, slap him around a little, make it clear if he doesn't play nice the next visit is going to involve broken kneecaps.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Beat him up in one RD and then walk into his Sanctum in another RD and pretend to help him. In the helpful RD suggest that maybe he shouldn't piss off so many people. You catch more flies with honey. Especially if you expose said flies to vinegar first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:32:46-07:00","id":561213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/561088-a-little-political-sidereal-guidance-in-the-campaign-i-am-in-please?p=561198#post561198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You catch more flies with honey. Especially if you expose said flies to vinegar first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Between this and the earlier snafu with Disguise of the New Face, you're just full of misconceptions, hm? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (That is to say, a good bowl of balsamic vinegar will draw a crapton more flies than mere honey.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:37:07-07:00","id":561216,"title":"","content":"The Yozi (plural) are not pleased with your lack of knowledge about proverbs, no matter how factually inaccurate they are. :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Chicanery-No: If a player uses this Charm in an abusive or exploitative manner, the ST may punch him right in the goddamn face.&quot; --TheDementedOne<br /> <br /> &quot;Happiness is <i>very</i> brittle and short-lived in the Exalted community, because <i>ressentiment</i> is our cultural touchstone.&quot; --Gayo","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3420-zelbinnean","name":"Zelbinnean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3420_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5884"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T14:40:12-07:00","id":561219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/561088-a-little-political-sidereal-guidance-in-the-campaign-i-am-in-please?p=561213#post561213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Between this and the earlier snafu with Disguise of the New Face, you're just full of misconceptions, hm? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (That is to say, a good bowl of balsamic vinegar will draw a crapton more flies than mere honey.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Hey! You are lucky I'm not posting in Linux commands and SQL queries.<br /> <br /> And a quick google search on what gets more flies, honey and vinegar gave me this: <a href=\"http://xkcd.com/357/\" target=\"_blank\">http://xkcd.com/357/</a><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-19T15:21:36-07:00","id":561272,"title":"","content":"I'm a tad confused on the scenario. What kind of message are you expected to send?How is the guy causing problems? Burning the guy's temple is probably excessive for inconveniencing the Sid. Hell one thing you could do is basically collect a list of the God's infractions get evidence, basically write up the whole thing and have it ready to get the guy audited and make it known to him that he either cleans up or it goes through the rest of the channels.<br /> <br /> Heck I'm gonna take a guess and say you lacking social charms means you have a decent amount of combat ability. Just show up inform him you're working a job and noticed the infractions because they're making your job harder than it needs to be. Then you simply put the lean that if doesn't stop you'll consider him getting in the way of the job and will need to be dealt with appropriately. Just make it clear that you're giving him the clean up chance because he's only getting a little out of hand and if it was more severe then you would have already moved on to proper punishment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}